    device Device
    doc_create_intro_desc This tab covers how creators organize content, localize it, and publish useful study material without overcomplicating the workflow.
    doc_create_intro_title Create
    doc_create_json_desc JSON-based creation is an advanced workflow for structured bulk content. It should remain optional; most creators should be able to build and edit content through the standard forms.
    doc_create_json_title Advanced JSON Import
    doc_create_localization_desc Localize content where it matters most: names, descriptions, prompts, and answers. Keep labels consistent across languages so users can switch study language without losing structure.
    doc_create_localization_title Localization
    doc_create_media_desc Images, audio, and video should support the learning goal, not distract from it. Add media when it improves recognition, pronunciation, or context, and keep cards usable even when media is missing.
    doc_create_media_title Media Workflow
    doc_create_model_desc Creators work inside pillars and organize material with folders, subjects, collections, and cards. Build the structure first, then fill it with localized prompts, answers, and optional media.
    doc_create_model_title Content Model
    doc_create_visibility_desc Use "mine" to work on your own content, favorites to pin useful items, and public library to browse shared material. Public visibility affects discovery, while ownership affects what you can edit or delete.
    doc_create_visibility_title Ownership and Visibility
    doc_start_dashboard_desc The dashboard is your main library. Use search to find content quickly, then combine source filters such as favorites, mine, and public library with age filters to reduce noise.
    doc_start_dashboard_title Dashboard, Search, and Filters
    doc_start_feedback_desc Use the feedback entry points across the app when something is wrong or unclear. Reports can include the current context, which makes content issues easier to review and fix.
    doc_start_feedback_title Feedback and Help
    doc_start_intro_desc Use this tab when you are learning how the dashboard, library, progress, and social features fit together.
    doc_start_intro_title Getting Started
    doc_start_progress_desc Your profile shows total XP, current streak, max streak, and daily goal progress. Session size and number of answers are also managed from the profile page.
    doc_start_progress_title Progress and Goals
    doc_start_quick_desc Pick a pillar on the dashboard, open a subject, and start with Learn. Use favorites and filters to narrow the library, then review your XP, streaks, and daily goal from your profile.
    doc_start_quick_title Quick Start
    doc_start_structure_desc Subjects hold cards. Folders group related content inside a pillar. Collections are curated sets that can combine multiple subjects for study and sharing.
    doc_start_structure_title Subjects, Folders, and Collections
    doc_study_how_desc Start with Learn when you are building recognition, then switch to Test when you want faster recall and stricter checking. Use shorter sessions for focused review and larger sessions for broader coverage.
    doc_study_how_title How to Study
    doc_study_intro_desc This tab explains how to move through content, choose the right mode, and tune your sessions for review or recall.
    doc_study_intro_title Study
    doc_study_media_desc When media is available, use it to reinforce pronunciation and recognition. Autoplay is most useful for passive review or repeated listening during shorter sessions.
    doc_study_media_title Audio, Autoplay, and Media
    doc_study_modes_desc Learn and Test are the core study modes. They use the same content but support different pacing and answer expectations, so switch modes based on whether you are exploring or checking retention.
    doc_study_modes_title Learn and Test Modes
    doc_study_scope_desc Study can start from a single subject, a folder view, or a collection. Collections are useful when you want a mixed session across several subjects without leaving the current flow.
    doc_study_scope_title Subjects, Folders, and Collections in Study
